| Scenario | Behavior |
|---|---|
| No args, valid stdin | Sorts records, writes to stdout, exit 0, empty stderr |
| Empty stdin | Empty stdout, exit 0, empty stderr |
| `-x`, `--foo` (any option) | "invalid option" + usage on stderr, exit 2, empty stdout |
| Bare `-`, `file.txt` (any operand) | "extra operand" + usage on stderr, exit 2, empty stdout |
| `--` alone | Accepted (end-of-options), proceeds to sort stdin |
| `-- file.txt` | `--` accepted, `file.txt` is operand → exit 2 |
| NUL bytes, invalid UTF-8, empty records | Handled as arbitrary bytes, sorted bytewise |
| Unterminated final record | Treated as a record, output gets trailing newline |
| `MemoryError` / `OSError` | Caught, diagnostic on stderr, exit 2 |
| Duplicates | Preserved (stable not required, duplicates kept) |

